{"context":"- Review 20 §2.3 item 2 classified the diagnostics surface as partially consistent: *lifecycle observability* — what is active, what can roll back, release status, state queries — is convention observation and required by the domain; *platform ops* — system health, readiness, recommendations breadth — is platform-ambition surface. The review's instruction: keep lifecycle observability, demote system-health/readiness breadth.\n- The Anvil V2 Transition Plan carries the Server Runtime trim in A9 / ADR-031 but assigns no ADR row to the diagnostics demotion (§8); ADR-031 §7 explicitly excludes it (\"a separate demotion\"). The QA assessment recorded the gap as RFC-01 (24-adr-quality-assessment §5).\n- Diagnostics is the observation surface of the convention: lifecycle state is persisted, queryable Source: ADR-036-diagnostics-scope-alignment.md Date:2026-08-03 Status:Proposed.","decision":"- **Diagnostics is scoped to lifecycle observability.** The v2 diagnostics surface exists to observe the lifecycle convention: what is active, what is installed, what can roll back, release status, and state queries. This is the observation pillar of convention-as-product (ANVIL_V2_TRANSITION_PLAN §1.1; ANVIL_MANIFESTO §4.1).\n- **The platform-ops breadth is demoted.** System-health/readiness breadth and recommendations-style diagnostics are not a v2 platform surface (Review 20 §2.3 item 2). They are neither removed from the product line nor expanded; they are demoted to optional, non-governing diagnostics that must never become a dependency of lifecycle operations.\n- **Lifecycle operations never depend on diagnostics.** Observability is read-only; no lifecycle transition requires a diagnos","consequences":"- **Positive:** the observation pillar has an explicit contractual home; the platform-ops breadth is bounded; lifecycle operations remain independent of diagnostics; the review-20 demotion is fully disposed across ADR-031 + ADR-036.\n- **Negative:** some v1.x diagnostics output (system health/readiness breadth) is demoted or removed — a governed surface change at implementation; documentation and the command-implementation checklist are aligned (EPIC-019, plan §7).","alternativesConsidered":"Considered\n\n- **Keep the full v1.x diagnostics breadth.** Rejected: it is platform-ambition surface (Review 20 §2.3 item 2) and re-introduces what ADR-031 demotes from the runtime.\n- **Remove diagnostics entirely.** Rejected: lifecycle observability is the observation pillar — state must remain queryable (ANVIL_MANIFESTO §3.3, §4.1; ANVIL_V2_TRANSITION_PLAN §2.2).\n- **Defer without a home.** Rejected: the QA assessment requires the disposition before implementation planning (24-adr-quality-asses"}